{"body": "Tested 2026-11-20, all HTTP 200 with User-Agent 'fein-research admin@example.com', no key. (1) data.sec.gov/submissions/CIK##########.json - company metadata (SIC, FYE, tickers, former names) and last ~1,000 filings with form, date, accession, 8-K items, primary doc; older history in paged files. (2) data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK##########.json - every XBRL fact ever filed (Apple: 3.9MB) with start/end, form, fiscal period, filed date, accession, so restated values and as-first-reported values are both recoverable. (3) companyconcept/CIK/us-gaap/TAG.json - one line item. (4) frames/us-gaap/TAG/USD/CY2024.json - one item across all filers (Revenues CY2024: 2,513 filers; NetIncomeLoss CY2025: 5,723) = free cross-sectional screen. Gotchas: frames contain filer scaling errors (one CY2025 NetIncomeLoss value was $1.157 trillion); companies switch tags (Revenues -> RevenueFromContractWithCustomer...); 10-Q cash flows are year-to-date; fiscal Q4 is not filed separately. Archives: www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/CIK/ACCNODASH/index.json lists filing files. Ticker map: www.sec.gov/files/company_tickers.json. Limit 10 req/s. Wrapped by tools/sec_fetch.py.", "confidence": "verified", "created": "2026-11-20T04:26:24Z", "data": {"auth": "none, descriptive UA required", "rate_limit": "10 req/s", "tested": "2026-11-20", "tool": "tools/sec_fetch.py"}, "date": "2026-11-20", "id": "source:sec-edgar-apis", "sources": ["https://www.sec.gov/search-filings/edgar-application-programming-interfaces", "https://www.sec.gov/os/accessing-edgar-data", "https://data.sec.gov/submissions/CIK0000320193.json"], "tags": ["us", "process", "data-access"], "title": "SEC EDGAR JSON APIs (submissions, companyfacts, companyconcept, frames) - free, tested", "type": "source", "updated": "2026-11-20T04:26:24Z", "version": 1}
